= BITwiki Dependency Schema =

== Purpose ==

Proactive tracking of transclusion dependencies using SMW properties to detect circular references before they cause parse failures.

== Property Definitions ==

=== Property:Depends on ===

[[Has type::Page]]
[[Has description::Template or fragment that this artifact depends on]]
[[Has property scope::Template, Fragment]]

=== Property:Required by ===

[[Has type::Page]]
[[Has description::Templates or fragments that depend on this artifact]]
[[Has property scope::Template, Fragment]]

=== Property:Has dependency depth ===

[[Has type::Number]]
[[Has description::Maximum depth of dependency chain from this artifact]]
[[Has property scope::Template, Fragment]]

== Template Integration ==

Add to each template's  section:

<pre>

[[Has entity type::Concept]]
[[Depends on::Template:Infobox Core]]
[[Depends on::Module:Validation]]

</pre>

== Fragment Integration ==

Add to each fragment:

<pre>
<onlyinclude>
...content...
</onlyinclude>
[[Depends on::Template:Infobox Concept]]
[[Has fragment level::L1]]
</pre>

== Circular Detection Query ==

Detect potential circular dependencies:

<pre>
{{#ask: [[Depends on::{{PAGENAME}}]]
|?Depends on
|format=table
|limit=50
}}
</pre>

== Dependency Chain Query ==

Trace full dependency chain:

<pre>
{{#ask: [[Depends on::+]]
|?Depends on
|?Required by
|format=table
|limit=100
}}
</pre>

== Validation Rules ==

= All templates must declare dependencies =
= No circular chains allowed (A → B → C → A) =
= Maximum dependency depth: 5 levels =
= Update dependencies when refactoring =
= Document breaking changes in talk page =

== Automated Checks ==

Pre-commit validation should:
= Parse all [[Depends on::]] declarations =
= Build dependency graph =
= Detect cycles using DFS =
= Report depth violations =

== Breaking Change Protocol ==

When removing or renaming a dependency:
= Update all dependent templates first =
= Add redirect if renaming =
= Document in [[BITwiki Changelog]] =
= Notify via [[Category:Breaking Changes]] =

